{"meta":{"format_version":"4.10","model_format":"free","box_uv":false},"name":"lair_great_barrow","model_identifier":"lair_great_barrow","visible_box":[1,1,0],"variable_placeholders":"","variable_placeholder_buttons":[],"timeline_setups":[],"unhandled_root_fields":{"description":"# lair_great_barrow\n\nLair: great barrow (C6, later undead; its own lair type, lairs never grow).\n\nA bigger barrow: a six-tier grassy mound 104 u high with a tall stone doorway (84 u opening) and turf cap, a dark passage with a faint blue glow (`glow_inner`), a paved approach, a collapsed stone tomb to its right (two uprights and a back slab with the cracked capstone slid off onto the ground, bones inside), and a ring of eight mossy standing stones around it. Footprint 16 x 14 terrain columns (256 x 224 u), centred on the origin, front (entrance) toward -Z.\n\n- Cubes: 31 (all unrotated unless noted). Texture 64x64, 1 px per unit, embedded.\n- Rest bounds (body, no held items): x -156.7..156.7, y 0.0..106.0, z -142.0..146.0 (faces -Z).\n\n## Hit box\n\n- mound: 210 x 106 x 170 (w x h x d) centred on x = 0, z = 20, from y = 0\n- doorway: 80 x 106 x 28 centred on x = 0, z = -63\n- tomb: 52 x 34 x 54 centred on x = 86, z = -84\n- standing stones: 13 x 58-78 x 10 each on a ring of radius ~150 x 130 around (0, 10)\n\n## Clips\n\n| clip | length (s) | loop | notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n\n## Attachment points (empty groups, pivot in model units)\n\n- `fx_spawn` on `root` at (0, 0, -75)\n- `fx_spawn_tomb` on `root` at (92, 0, -90)\n- `fx_glow` on `root` at (0, 40, -51)\n\n## Notes\n\n- `fx_spawn`: main doorway threshold; `fx_spawn_tomb`: the open tomb (a second spawn); `fx_glow`: inside the passage (faint blue light).\n- Lit cube: glow_inner.\n- Destroyed version: `lair_great_barrow_destroyed.bbmodel` in this folder (separate file, same footprint).\n"},"description":"# lair_great_barrow\n\nLair: great barrow (C6, later undead; its own lair type, lairs never grow).\n\nA bigger barrow: a six-tier grassy mound 104 u high with a tall stone doorway (84 u opening) and turf cap, a dark passage with a faint blue glow (`glow_inner`), a paved approach, a collapsed stone tomb to its right (two uprights and a back slab with the cracked capstone slid off onto the ground, bones inside), and a ring of eight mossy standing stones around it. Footprint 16 x 14 terrain columns (256 x 224 u), centred on the origin, front (entrance) toward -Z.\n\n- Cubes: 31 (all unrotated unless noted). Texture 64x64, 1 px per unit, embedded.\n- Rest bounds (body, no held items): x -156.7..156.7, y 0.0..106.0, z -142.0..146.0 (faces -Z).\n\n## Hit box\n\n- mound: 210 x 106 x 170 (w x h x d) centred on x = 0, z = 20, from y = 0\n- doorway: 80 x 106 x 28 centred on x = 0, z = -63\n- tomb: 52 x 34 x 54 centred on x = 86, z = -84\n- standing stones: 13 x 58-78 x 10 each on a ring of radius ~150 x 130 around (0, 10)\n\n## Clips\n\n| clip | length (s) | loop | notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n\n## Attachment points (empty groups, pivot in model units)\n\n- `fx_spawn` on `root` at (0, 0, -75)\n- `fx_spawn_tomb` on `root` at (92, 0, -90)\n- `fx_glow` on `root` at (0, 40, -51)\n\n## Notes\n\n- `fx_spawn`: main doorway threshold; `fx_spawn_tomb`: the open tomb (a second spawn); `fx_glow`: inside the passage (faint blue light).\n- Lit cube: glow_inner.\n- Destroyed version: `lair_great_barrow_destroyed.bbmodel` in this folder (separate file, same footprint).\n","resolution":{"width":512,"height":1024},"elements":[{"name":"mound_0","box_uv":false,"rescale":false,"locked":false,"light_emission":0,"render_order":"default","allow_mirror_modeling":true,"from":[-105.0,0.0,-65.0],"to":[105.0,21.666666666666664,105.0],"autouv":0,"color":0,"inflate":0.0,"origin":[0.0,0.0,0.0],"faces":{"north":{"uv":[246,446,456.0,467.6666666666667],"texture":0},"east":{"uv":[210,472,380.0,493.6666666666667],"texture":0},"south":{"uv":[0,472,210.0,493.6666666666667],"texture":0},"west":{"uv":[0,494,170.0,515.6666666666666],"texture":0